@startuml DLT Log Analyzer — Sequence Diagram
title DLT Log Analyzer — End-to-End Sequence (CLI MVP)

actor Developer as Dev
participant "CLI Orchestrator" as CLI
participant "DLT Parser" as Parser
participant "Parsed Log Store (JSON)" as ParsedStore
participant "Feature Extractor" as Features
participant "Log Vector DB (FAISS)" as LogVectorDB
participant "Code Chunk Index" as CodeIndex
participant "Classifier (SVM/LightGBM)" as Classifier
participant "Retriever (Vector Search)" as Retriever
participant "Re-ranker (LightGBM)" as Ranker
participant "Explanation Composer" as Explain
participant "Local Storage (.json/sqlite)" as LocalStore
participant "Labels / Feedback Store" as Labels
participant "Retrain Service" as Retrain
participant "LLM Service (optional)" as LLM
participant "Static Analysis (optional)" as Static
participant "Symbol / Build Map (optional)" as Symbol

== User runs CLI ==
Dev -> CLI : run_analysis --file <dlt> --output results.json
CLI -> Parser : parse <dlt> file
Parser -> ParsedStore : write parsed JSON (structured logs)
ParsedStore --> CLI : ack (parsed path)

== Feature extraction & indexing/checks ==
CLI -> Features : request features for parsed log
Features -> ParsedStore : read parsed window (N lines)
Features -> LogVectorDB : compute & upsert embeddings (optional)
Features -> CodeIndex : (if code not indexed) ensure index available
CodeIndex --> Features : confirm index ready
Features --> CLI : return feature vector + metadata

== Initial predictions & retrieval ==
CLI -> Classifier : predict candidate modules (top-K)
Classifier --> CLI : candidate modules + scores
CLI -> Retriever : embed log query and search
Retriever -> LogVectorDB : query top similar logs
Retriever -> CodeIndex : query top matching code chunks
LogVectorDB --> Retriever : return similar past incidents
CodeIndex --> Retriever : return top code chunks
Retriever --> CLI : return retrieval results

== Ranking & explanation ==
CLI -> Ranker : assemble candidate list (classifier + retrieval) and score
Ranker --> CLI : ranked candidates (top-3) with internal scores
CLI -> Explain : provide ranked candidates + retrieved evidence
alt If LLM enabled
  Explain -> LLM : send evidence-only payload (low temp; JSON schema)
  LLM --> Explain : formatted explanations (strict evidence-based)
else
  Explain --> CLI : format explanation from evidence (no LLM)
end
Explain -> LocalStore : save results and evidence
LocalStore --> CLI : results.json ready
CLI --> Dev : print results.json (top-3 candidates + evidence + confidence)

== Optional: run static analysis on top candidate ==
opt If static analysis desired
  Dev -> CLI : request deeper check (candidate idx)
  CLI -> Static : run_static_analysis(file, lines)
  Static --> CLI : static report (warnings/errors)
  CLI -> Explain : append static report to evidence
  CLI --> Dev : updated results
end

== Feedback loop (learning) ==
Dev -> Labels : submit feedback (approved / correct_file / notes)
Labels --> Retrain : new labeled data
Retrain -> Classifier : retrain baseline model (periodic)
Retrain -> Ranker : retrain ranker (periodic)
Retrain --> LocalStore : store new model artifacts
LocalStore --> CLI : update models used for inference

== Optional: Symbol/build map assistance ==
opt If symbol/build mapping available
  Symbol -> CodeIndex : push mapping (messageID -> source file)
  CodeIndex --> Ranker : boost candidates with mapping matches
end

note over Ranker,Explain
Recommendations:
- Keep LLM calls evidence-only.
- Enforce deterministic outputs: low temperature, strict JSON schema.
- Always show raw matched log lines & code snippets to developers.
end note

@enduml
